WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.344 --> 00:00:13.722
I will skip the part
where I brag for three minutes

00:00:13.805 --> 00:00:15.641
about how great and cool I am.

00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:18.435
Seeing as we are all qualified young men

00:00:18.519 --> 00:00:20.103
of skill and character.

00:00:20.187 --> 00:00:21.772
-People like that stuff.
-Sounds good, yeah.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:22.856
People like that stuff a lot.

00:00:26.527 --> 00:00:29.196
Some people say they're a sports junkie,
I say, "I'm a politics junkie."

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.340
The harder the conflict,
the more glorious the triumph.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.660
I'm playing this like a game.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.120
I would like very much to win.

00:00:35.202 --> 00:00:36.495
I love it, boys, I love it. Where you from?

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.039
I come from a very modest family.

00:00:39.122 --> 00:00:41.542
I'm on the course to be the first one
to graduate from high school.

00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:43.544
I'm a progressive person,

00:00:43.627 --> 00:00:46.296
and I'm in a room full
of mostly conservative people.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:49.758
Our masculinity shall not be infringed.

00:00:51.176 --> 00:00:53.679
I've never seen so many white people, ever.

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:57.015
I feel like everybody has
this secret underlying need

00:00:57.099 --> 00:00:58.267
for bipartisanship.

00:01:01.937 --> 00:01:06.692
A message of unity, as good as it sounds,
is not winning anyone any elections.

00:01:09.695 --> 00:01:12.406
Primary polls are now open.

00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:15.325
Get yourselves ready
for a turbulent election.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.080
Whatever happens to you, best of luck.

00:01:20.163 --> 00:01:21.832
You'll win. I support you fully.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.000
My name is Steven Garza,

00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:25.419
and I'm running for governor.

00:01:28.714 --> 00:01:30.799
A special applause because...

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:34.303
As to the political views
voiced in my speech,

00:01:34.386 --> 00:01:37.222
sometimes you gotta say what you gotta say
in an attempt to win.

00:01:37.306 --> 00:01:39.349
I think he's a fantastic politician.

00:01:40.392 --> 00:01:43.437
But I don't think "a fantastic politician"
is a compliment either.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.606
Yeah! Yeah!

00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:47.900
We're gonna do shock and awe.
It's gonna be awesome.

00:01:47.983 --> 00:01:50.027
I want you all to take out your phones

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.987
and go on Instagram. Everyone, come on.

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.113
Oh, my God!

00:02:00.871 --> 00:02:03.665
We show the world what patriots are made of,

00:02:04.041 --> 00:02:05.792
that when things get tough,

00:02:05.876 --> 00:02:07.878
we pull ourselves by our bootstraps,

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.838
one nation under God,

00:02:09.922 --> 00:02:13.425
lovers of the Constitution
of the United States of America!

00:02:15.719 --> 00:02:17.513
That's politics, I think.

00:02:18.055 --> 00:02:19.056
That's politics.

